# CODEOWNERS defines who is automatically requested to review pull requests.
#
# How it works:
#   - Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more GitHub usernames or teams.
#   - The last matching pattern wins, so more specific rules below override broader ones above.
#   - Owners are automatically added as reviewers when a PR touches matching files.
#   - Review from a code owner can be made required via branch protection settings:
#     Settings → Branches → Require review from Code Owners.
#
# Pattern syntax (same as .gitignore):
#   *        matches any file in the repo (root catch-all)
#   src/     matches everything under the src/ directory
#   *.ts     matches all TypeScript files anywhere in the repo
#
# Examples:
#   *                    @alice @bob          # all files
#   src/payments/        @payments-team       # a subdirectory
#   *.sql                @dba-team            # all SQL files

